ally to fold weak hands to avoid losing chips unnecessarily. Raising or checking (since no bet yet) would commit chips with a hand that has low equity against a random opponent hand. All-in is far too aggressive and reckless with this holding.\n\nReason: Pre-flop strategy in Texas Hold’em typically involves folding low suited connectors or weak suited cards when out of position unless getting very good pot odds or in a blind scenario. Here, checking is an option, but it risks being raised by the opponent, putting you in a tough spot later. Folding preserves chips for better opportunities. Raising is not justified given the hand strength.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
